## Conclusion

In this experiment, we created a child process using the `fork()` system call and displayed its PID. We used `getpid()` and `getppid()` to identify the parent and child processes. We also used the `wait()` system call to make the parent process wait until the child process terminates. Thus, we understood process creation and synchronization in Linux.
